    "answer": {
      "short": "Green: $\\frac13$, $120^\\circ$; Red: $\\frac5{18}$, $100^\\circ$; Yellow: $\\frac1{18}$, $20^\\circ$; Purple: $\\frac1{12}$, $30^\\circ$; Brown: $\\frac1{12}$, $30^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Divide each frequency by 720 to find its fraction of the students. Multiply that fraction by $360^\\circ$ to find the sector angle.\n\nGreen: $\\frac{240}{720}=\\frac13$, so $\\frac13\\times360^\\circ=120^\\circ$.\n\nRed: $\\frac{200}{720}=\\frac5{18}$, so $\\frac5{18}\\times360^\\circ=100^\\circ$.\n\nYellow: $\\frac{40}{720}=\\frac1{18}$, so $\\frac1{18}\\times360^\\circ=20^\\circ$.\n\nPurple and Brown each have $\\frac{60}{720}=\\frac1{12}$, so each sector is $\\frac1{12}\\times360^\\circ=30^\\circ$.\n\nDraw a circle and use a protractor to construct the six sectors. Label each sector with its colour. The angles total $60^\\circ+120^\\circ+100^\\circ+20^\\circ+30^\\circ+30^\\circ=360^\\circ$.",
